<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5312"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 4:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you Essevi.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5312-->
<!--Post: 5581--><!--Time: 1107204776-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5581"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 12:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if any of the victims&#39; homes were located on a &#34;drive test route&#34;.  Conceivably when giving a drive test you could pass by the same house &#40;homes&#41; about 20 times a day. In most instances there is a regular route and an alternate route &#40;that would be used if a person failed the test on the regular route or if there was a detour due to road construction or the like&#41;.  In California &#40;don&#39;t know about Kansas&#41; a railroad crossing must be a mandatory part of the drive test, specifically when administering Class 1 or Class 2 drive tests.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5581-->
<!--Post: 5592--><!--Time: 1107211716-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5592"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clairevoient<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clairevoient<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 2:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linnieskid is on fire! <BR> <BR>We need KS DMV information from a Wichita DMV insider. Anybody? <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll start a wish list. <BR> <BR>Confirmation on 1970s procedures, uniforms, badges and frequency of field test requirements for licensees. <BR> <BR>When did Joe, Julie, Kathy, Shirley, Nancy Jo and Vicki take their final driving exams in Wichita? <BR> <BR>Wouldn&#39;t a DMV employee be required to photocopy and file an applicant&#39;s alternate photo I.D. in order to process a lost license replacement? Or for special government or commercial driver&#39;s permits for, say, school or utility company employees?  <BR> <BR>Would the local DMV be responsible in any way for documenting Joe&#39;s injury accident? <BR> <BR>Did DMV examiners moonlight at driving schools? <BR> <BR>&#34;Pull over to the shoulder in front of this white house and execute a 3-point-turn please. <BR>Yes, the white house. That is correct. <BR>Relax.  <BR>Take your time.” <BR> <BR>“Good Morning Ma’am. I’m Officer Killman with the State Department of Motor Vehicles. Your husband was recently involved in a collision…  <BR>Yes, I just need his signature for…  <BR>I see….  <BR>Well, when will he be… I see. <BR>Would you mind if I wait inside then? It’s awfully cold today… <BR>Oh thank you… Thank you very much.  <BR> <BR>Better check your rear view mirror, B_ _T_ _ _K®. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5592-->
<!--Post: 5598--><!--Time: 1107213432-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5598"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 3:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linnieskid, as a variation of your &#39;test drive&#39; DMV drivers license route which certainly is plausable may I add to it another possiblity of being a route for test driving a new car from an auto dealer. Take the new car for a spin past victims homes and end up not buying the car.  <BR>Didn&#39;t mean to get away from the DMV angle, just that the test drive reminded me of another kind of test drive.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5598-->
<!--Post: 5601--><!--Time: 1107215483-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5601"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 3:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What is the closest DMV center near the crime scenes? <BR> <BR>Since Johno brought it up first.  <BR>A buddy of mine is a mechanic and he test drives different cars every single day but he likes to take the same route for his test drives. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5601-->
<!--Post: 5603--><!--Time: 1107216026-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5603"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 4:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, Perfectly plausible! &#40;watching without being seen&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5603-->
<!--Post: 5606--><!--Time: 1107216697-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5606"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 4:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->clairvoient- your scenario is too creepy! One never knows; could have happened just like that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5606-->
<!--Post: 5625--><!--Time: 1107221513-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5625"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clairevoient<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clairevoient<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 5:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My hat is off to Metalhead and to you for helping me to see it this way. <BR> <BR>You also made me see how he could easily collect the type of picture I.D.s that he revealed in  his May communication.   <BR> <BR>C&#39;mon Wichita! Who here knows a DMV insider?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5625-->
<!--Post: 5802--><!--Time: 1107385257-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5802"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 3:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a completely wonderful suggestion.  However, we all know that the most likeliest of ideas can inevitably be the most unlikeliest of reality.  I think you are more on track with the DMV suggestion.  I believe, because of such tragic murders, all suggestions should be considered for a moment at least.  Well, what if &#40;what if now&#41;,BTK was familiar with the University because he was somewhat involved with taking pictures for student identification cards?  I know that is a standard practice where I attend college today, but I do not know if it was during the time of the murders.  Does anybody know if that was a standard practice at that time, and did any of the victims recently have a picture taken for any reason for university purposes?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5802-->
<!--Post: 5826--><!--Time: 1107392648-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5826"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 5:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I went to Case Western in Ohio in 1976 and pic taking was not that big of a thing if you needed to use something of the Universitys&#39; you either showed a drivers license or student ID,I was never asked for my student ID in the library because there was always some sort of asst. there doing work for either a lawyer or doctor.Now you can&#39;t even get on campus without it.They had a couple rapes on the campus in 85 and that is when it changed.Not real sure about WSU but I think all security was pretty lax back then.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5826-->
<!--Post: 6006--><!--Time: 1107478388-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6006"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 4:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have two friends that used to work for the DMV.  AKA Drivers License office.  The still wear uniforms today, looks like the Kansas Highway Patrol uniforms, except for the crazy RCMP had.  Today they are blue shirts and pants with a blue stripe, with black shoes.  I got my driver&#39;s license in the armory down the street from the Otero home in 1977, and I am nearly certain that they were wearing uniforms then, however, I do not remember the color. I am also certain that there were only two offices in Wichita at the time, both at the National Guard Armories.  The other one was on South Seneca.  Seneca, funny how that comes up again, huh?  I am also a student at WSU, and they have student employees take the pictures.  It has been done this way since at least 1989.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6006-->
<!--Post: 6010--><!--Time: 1107479385-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6010"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 5:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just thought of something else.  The Kansas Department of Revenue that issues driver&#39;s licenses in Kansas changed to a system using either your social security number or a K00-00-0000 number that they assign.  I think that was in the late 80&#39;s early 90&#39;s.  Before that the numbers were alpha, number, alpha, number, alpha, number.  Just an example B4L8C5.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6010-->
<!--Post: 6517--><!--Time: 1107849290-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6517"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Toto<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Toto<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 11:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi all, I&#39;m new to posting, but not this case.  Thought I&#39;d help out.   <BR> <BR>Lmuncy316 - No pics were on the WSU ID cards from 78 - 82 when I was a student.  Regarding  security on campus; it was extremely tight then.  There&#39;d been a murder in the girls dorm &#40;Brennan Hall&#41; the spring of 78 &#40;Julie Ladd&#41;.  I was a freshman the following fall.  The &#39;buddy&#39; system was in full force then.   You couldn&#39;t travel alone on campus after dark.  If you didn&#39;t have a &#39;buddy&#39; you called campus security and they&#39;d walk you to your car, building, dorm, bus stop, etc.        <BR> <BR>Purple - you&#39;re right about the armories being the DVM where you&#39;d go get your license, also the number/letter combo.  KS started using picture DL&#39;s in 76.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6517-->
<!--Post: 6876--><!--Time: 1108059379-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6876"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 10:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Toto, <BR> <BR>Thank you for the information.  What type of access do you have to Wichita State University yearbooks, or Wichita high school yearbooks.  I visited the Wichita State web site and could not find what I was looking for.  If you could provide me with a link or information on buying yearbooks of the past I would be more than interested in purchasing them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6876-->
<!--Post: 6976--><!--Time: 1108100670-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6976"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:tbjostad@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Toto<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Toto<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 9:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah, WSU&#39;s site leaves alot to be desired when searching for info.  I still have library priveleges and will actually be there next week.  I&#39;m sure the yearbooks are there.  I don&#39;t know about ordering copies of old ones, but I can find out.  Not sure if I can check them out, but if there are certain years you&#39;d be interested in, I can certainly try.   <BR> <BR>As for HS yearbooks, those are probably available through the Wichita Public Library - to which I also have access.  Which school&#40;s&#41; and years are you interested in?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6976-->
<!--Post: 7288--><!--Time: 1108366677-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7288"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 11:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->hey metalhead i like your dmv idea. <BR>if you look a map of all the killings, coleman buildings,murdock park etc. hillside and douglas is right in the center. <BR>the building that is there used to be a state building, 3244 east douglas. <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/2005/01/28/business/10753194.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/2005/01/28/busine ss/10753194.htm</a> does anyone know did it ever house dmv or dmv records. just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7288-->
</table></td></tr></table>
